msgid "About Quarkus documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A detailed reference for the structure and composition of Quarkus "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Source locations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus doc sources are built and synced to the https://quarkus.io/guides/"
"[Quarkus.io website] at release time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Documentation for Quarkus core and most extensions is located in the `docs` "
"module of the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/tree/main/docs[Quarkus "
"GitHub repository]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Docs for Quarkiverse or other third-party extensions are pulled directly "
"from those repositories."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Asciidoc files can be found in the `src/main/asciidoc` directory within "
"the docs module."
msgstr ""

msgid "Templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create new documentation files using the appropriate template for the "
"content type:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Concepts"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-concepts.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "How-To Guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-howto.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-reference.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use `docs/src/main/asciidoc/_templates/template-tutorial.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Output locations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration references"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Javadoc comments discovered in MicroProfile Config source files are used to "
"generate config reference documentation.\n"
"These generated files are found in `target/asciidoc/generated/config/` (from "
"the project root)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Asciidoc output as HTML"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A locally-rendered result of asciidoc processing (which is similar, but not "
"identical, to that used to generate website documentation) is found in `docs/"
"target/generated-docs/`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Titles and headings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Regardless of content type, ensure that the main title and any headings in "
"your document are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Goal-oriented and use the language and keywords of the audience"
msgstr ""

msgid "Descriptive and avoid filler words"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Between 3-12 words and 50-80 characters per line to optimize findability in "
"search engines"
msgstr ""

msgid "In sentence case capitalization style"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your titles and headings must also follow the specific guidance for the "
"Quarkus content types, as outlined in the following table:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Title guidance for different Quarkus content types"
msgstr ""

msgid "Content type"
msgstr ""

msgid "Should ..."
msgstr ""

msgid "Good example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Bad example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Concept"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Start with a noun that names the concept or topic\n"
"* Never start with an active verb, for example, an action word like "
"configure, install, or start\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"Understanding … \""
msgstr ""

msgid "Start with a noun that names the concept or topic"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Never start with an active verb, for example, an action word like configure, "
"install, or start"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"Understanding … \""
msgstr ""

msgid "Security and authentication mechanisms in Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid "Discovering Reactive SQL Clients In Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid "How-To Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Start with an active verb in the imperative verb form, for example, "
"‘Create a ...’ or ‘Secure a ...’\n"
"* Be action-oriented or task-oriented, rather than feature-oriented\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"How to..\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Start with an active verb in the imperative verb form, for example, ‘Create "
"a ...’ or ‘Secure a ...’"
msgstr ""

msgid "Be action-oriented or task-oriented, rather than feature-oriented"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"How to..\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Secure your Quarkus application with WebAuthn authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid "Applying WebAuthn Authentication In Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Use a noun phrase to concisely summarize the content of the document\n"
"* Not include the word 'reference'\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"About ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Use a noun phrase to concisely summarize the content of the document"
msgstr ""

msgid "Not include the word 'reference'"
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"About ...\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate Reactive API configuration properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Reference guide for Configuring Hibernate Reactive API Configuration "
"Properties"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"* Start with an active verb in the imperative verb form, for example, "
"‘Create a ...’ or ‘Secure a ...’\n"
"* State what task the user will complete, with emphasis on the key topic or "
"demonstrated activity\n"
"* Be action-oriented or task-oriented, rather than feature-oriented\n"
"* Be led by the needs of the user in learning mode.\n"
"* Finish the implied sentence: \"In this tutorial, you will… \""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"State what task the user will complete, with emphasis on the key topic or "
"demonstrated activity"
msgstr ""

msgid "Be led by the needs of the user in learning mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Finish the implied sentence: \"In this tutorial, you will… \""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create a Quarkus application in JVM mode by using the quick start example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating an App"
msgstr ""

msgid "File naming conventions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus docs are stored in a fairly flat structure in an effort to make "
"things easier to discover.\n"
"The bulk of the file name should be some representation of its title.\n"
"Use all lowercase letters, separate words with hyphens, and don't use "
"symbols or special characters."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prefix"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use a common prefix to group related documents, e.g. all of the documents "
"related to writing Quarkus docs are prefixed with `doc-`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Suffix"
msgstr ""

msgid "The file name should reflect the type of document:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Concept documents should end in `-concepts.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "How-to guides should end in `-howto.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "References should end in `-reference.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tutorials should end in `-tutorial.adoc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Asciidoc syntax"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus docs use Asciidoc syntax.\n"
"The following links provide background on Asciidoc syntax and general "
"conventions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://redhat-documentation.github.io/asciidoc-markup-conventions/[AsciiDoc "
"Mark-up Quick Reference for Documentation]"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/[Asciidoctor User Manual]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/syntax-quick-reference/"
"[AsciiDoc Syntax Quick Reference]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Semantic line breaks"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Text in paragraphs, lists, and tables should be broken into pieces that are "
"easier to review{semantic-line-breaks}.\n"
"Start a new line at the end of each sentence, and split sentences themselves "
"at natural breaks between clauses."
msgstr ""

msgid "Abstracts (preamble)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For optimum findability, add a short description using user-oriented "
"keywords to summarize the document's purpose, task, and intent in no more "
"than three sentences.\n"
"Avoid self-referential expressions and filler words, such as \"This document."
".\", \"This tutorial..\", and \"The following..\"\n"
"Mentioning the benefits users gain from reading the content is also helpful."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first sentence of the abstract must explain the value and some benefit "
"of the content in less than 26 words because this automatically displays on "
"the link:https://quarkus.io/guides/[Quarkus guides homepage]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic Table of Contents (TOC)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `:toc: preamble` in the document header to insert an automatically "
"generated TOC after the abstract (or preamble) to the document.\n"
"For example, this document has the following in its header:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Using sections"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Section titles should be written in sentence case, rather than title case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All documents should start with a Title (a `= Level 0` heading), and should\n"
"be broken into subsections as appropriate\n"
"(`== Level 1` to `====== Level 5`)\n"
"without skipping any levels."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Deep nesting (`====== Level 4`, `====== Level 5`)\n"
"should be avoided whenever possible.\n"
"If you end up with deeply nested sections, think about the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Is this information in the right place?\n"
"For example, if this is a reference, should some of this content be moved to "
"a concept doc or how-to guide instead?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Can the content be re-organized to make it simpler to consume?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See xref:{doc-guides}/doc-concepts.adoc[Quarkus documentation concepts] for "
"more information about content types and organization."
msgstr ""

msgid "Links"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In general, prefer using https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/macros/"
"url-macro/[url macros] to using bare or automatic links.\n"
"Provide human-readable text for the link, especially if it is included in "
"the middle of other text."
msgstr ""

msgid "A URL Macro link with attributes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The URL macro also supports https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/latest/"
"macros/link-macro-ref/[additional attributes] that may be relevant, like "
"opening a link in a different window."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The above source produces this link: https://docs.asciidoctor.org/asciidoc/"
"latest/syntax-quick-reference/[Asciidoc Syntax Quick Reference,window="
"_blank,opts=nofollow]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-references"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus documentation is built from source in a few different environments.\n"
"We use attributes in our cross-references to ensure our docs can be built "
"across these environments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-reference source attributes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{code-examples}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to directory containing collected example source files"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{doc-guides}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to documentation adoc files (e.g. doc-concepts.adoc)"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{doc-examples}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to source examples for documentation guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{generated-dir}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to generated configuration `*.adoc` files"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{imagesdir}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Relative path to directory containing images"
msgstr ""

msgid "\\{includes}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Relative path to directory containing partial/reusable content (`*.adoc` "
"files)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When cross-referencing content, always use the inter-document `xref:` syntax "
"and supply a human-readable label to your link."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The cross reference starts with `xref:`, uses a cross-reference source "
"attribute(`\\{doc-guides}`), and provides a readable description: `[Quarkus "
"Documentation concepts]`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reference source code"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are many ways to include source code and examples in documentation."
msgstr ""

msgid "The simplest is to write it directly in the file, like this:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In documents like tutorials, you may want to reference source code that is "
"built and tested regularly.\n"
"The Quarkus documentation module build will copy source files enumerated in "
"`*-examples/yaml` files into a flattened structure in the `target/asciidoc/"
"examples` directory (from the project root)."
msgstr ""

msgid "define the path of source to be copied"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"define the simplified target file name to use when copying the file into the "
"`target/asciidoc/examples` directory. We recommend using the same prefix as "
"the related/consuming documentation in the file name."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Content copied in this way is referenced using the `\\{code-examples}` "
"source attribute. If a copied file contains the literal string `{{source}}`, "
"that literal value is replaced with the path of the source file."
msgstr ""

msgid "Micrometer example"
msgstr ""

msgid "The source file to be copied is:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`integration-tests/micrometer-prometheus/src/main/java/documentation/example/"
"telemetry/micrometer/tutorial/ExampleResource.java`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The target file name we want to use in docs is:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`telemetry-micrometer-tutorial-example-resource.java`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The source and target file names are declared in `docs/src/main/asciidoc/"
"telemetry-examples.yaml`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snippets from this source file are then included using the following path:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`\\{code-examples}/telemetry-micrometer-tutorial-example-resource.java`."
msgstr ""

